# Noble Path — Docker build context exclusions
#
# Two jobs here:
#   1. Keep the build context small and the image cache stable.
#   2. SECURITY: guarantee that no credential, no git history and no untracked
#      working material can ever end up inside a published image layer.
#
# Anything added to .gitignore that could contain a secret must also be added
# here. .gitignore protects the repository; this file protects the image.

# --- Secrets and local configuration (never in an image) ---------------------
# No .env file of any kind enters the build context — not even .env.example.
# Runtime configuration is injected by the platform, never baked into a layer.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
.vercel
.netlify

# --- Version control and CI --------------------------------------------------
.git
.gitignore
.github
.gitattributes

# --- Dependencies and build output (rebuilt inside the image) ----------------
node_modules
.next
out
build
dist
*.tsbuildinfo
.npm
.cache

# --- Working material not part of the application ----------------------------
# Unsorted source photography staged by the team. Large, unlicensed-by-default,
# and explicitly excluded from the repository in .gitignore. Never ship it.
untitled folder/
data/*.json

# --- Documentation and project meta (not needed at runtime) ------------------
docs
README.md
CHANGELOG.md
LICENSE

# --- Container and editor files ----------------------------------------------
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
docker-compose*.yml
.vscode
.idea

# --- OS noise ----------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# --- Logs --------------------------------------------------------------------
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
